{
  "id": "ep223",
  "duration": 51.302,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.996,
      "text": "A city-bus-sized asteroid snuck halfway inside our Moon's protective orbit.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "PIA21259 - Celestial Object 2016 WF9, a NEOWISE Discovery (Artist Concept).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL-Caltech",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PIA21259_-_Celestial_Object_2016_WF9,_a_NEOWISE_Discovery_(Artist_Concept).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 3.5,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 3.5,
          "end": 5.0,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.996,
      "end": 12.216,
      "text": "In February 2023, astronomers at the Canary Islands telescope spotted the unexpected visitor.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 5.0,
          "end": 12.2,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 12.216,
      "end": 18.736,
      "text": "Initial estimates showed a rock forty to ninety meters across, orbiting the Sun every three years.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 12.2,
          "end": 18.733,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 18.736,
      "end": 26.331,
      "text": "Worse yet, orbital calculations briefly flagged the object as a virtual impactor for March 2026.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "PIA21259 - Celestial Object 2016 WF9, a NEOWISE Discovery (Artist Concept).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL-Caltech",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PIA21259_-_Celestial_Object_2016_WF9,_a_NEOWISE_Discovery_(Artist_Concept).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 18.733,
          "end": 26.333,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 26.331,
      "end": 33.076,
      "text": "Alarm spread until further radar tracking completely ruled out any risk, removing it from threat lists.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Goldstone DSN antenna.jpg",
        "credit": "Unknown author",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Goldstone_DSN_antenna.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 26.333,
          "end": 33.067,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 33.076,
      "end": 40.921,
      "text": "On March 25, the fast-rotating space rock zoomed safely past at one hundred seventy-five thousand kilometers.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Released to Public Earth by NASA (NASA, GPN-2000-001437) (241635550).jpg",
        "credit": "pingnews.com",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Released_to_Public_Earth_by_NASA_(NASA,_GPN-2000-001437)_(241635550).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 33.067,
          "end": 40.933,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 40.921,
      "end": 47.441,
      "text": "Its extreme proximity allowed stargazers worldwide to track the object with small binoculars.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Young astronomy enthusiast looking at the moon through the SkyWatcher telescope.jpg",
        "credit": "Astroclubkosova",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Young_astronomy_enthusiast_looking_at_the_moon_through_the_SkyWatcher_telescope.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 40.933,
          "end": 47.433,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 47.441,
      "end": 50.952,
      "text": "Giving backyard telescopes a front-row view of the moment",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "PIA21259 - Celestial Object 2016 WF9, a NEOWISE Discovery (Artist Concept).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL-Caltech",
